Explanation of what these do:

1. We import the `ClickListener` helper so that we can detect clicks outside of our ComboBox.
2. We wrap the entire `<div className={wrapperClasses}>…</div>` in `<ClickListener onClickOutside={…}>…</ClickListener>`, and in that handler we call `toggleMenu(false)` any time the user clicks outside.  
3. As a result, whenever a ComboBox is open and the user clicks anywhere else on the page (including the toggle of another ComboBox), the first ComboBox will close before the next one opens.
